course: dictionary
lesson: 7900
title: Rarely and how often
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Rarely is an adverb. An adverb tells us more about a verb, and here it tells us how often something happens. Rarely means not often; almost never. «Money that is lost in the street is very rarely found again.» The word very makes it stronger: it is almost never found.
explain: Rarely sits between sometimes and never. Sometimes means now and then, rarely means hardly ever, and never means not at all. Try the swap test: «Sharks rarely bite people» still makes sense with «hardly ever» in its place, so rarely means almost never.
explain: Look for clues around the word. «Starting a club can help ... especially quiet children who are rarely asked.» If quiet children are rarely asked, they are hardly ever invited to join in. The clue is the idea of asking, and the meaning is about how often.
fact: Rarely means not often; almost never.
fact: Rarely is an adverb: it tells us how often something happens.
fact: Useful phrases are «rarely ever», «very rarely» and «only rarely».
fact: «Caimans rarely attack big grown capybaras, which are too big and alert.» This means the caimans almost never attack them.
fact: Rarely can also mean unusually, as in «a rarely beautiful day», but this is an older use.
exercise: «Sharks very rarely bite people.» What does rarely tell us? | *Not often; almost never | Always at night | Very loudly | Every single day
exercise: Which words mean the same as rarely? | Hardly ever | Next to nothing | Twice as often | *Seldom, almost never
exercise: In «Starting a club can help quiet children who are rarely asked», what does rarely mean? | Quickly | Always | *Hardly ever, so almost never | Hardly ever
test: «Money that is lost in the street is very rarely found again.» Which word tells how often the money is found? | Again | *Rarely | Found | Very
test: Ella says rarely means always. Is she right? | No, rarely means not often | *No, rarely means not often; almost never | Yes, it means loudly | Yes, it means always
exam: Jayden writes, «Caimans rarely attack big capybaras.» What does rarely tell us about the caimans? | Always attack them | *They almost never attack them | They attack them every day | They attack them at night only
